Perplexity's recommendations, and the study did not show that they changed which products Perplexity recommended. It did show that publishing content at volume for machine retrieval was enough to get some of it into the evidence an AI recommendation system works from.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-1\",id:\"user-content-fnref-1-2\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"1\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsx)(t.h2,{id:\"where-the-recommendations-come-from\",children:\"Where the recommendations come from\"}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://docs.perplexity.ai/api-reference/sonar-post\",children:\"Perplexity's Sonar models\"}),\" are built to ground answers in web content, and their API returns the search results and citation URLs behind an answer alongside the generated text. That makes them convenient to study.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-2\",id:\"user-content-fnref-2\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"2\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[\"Trellner defined 380 buyer-intent software categories, from CRM software to narrow vertical products, and asked both Sonar and Sonar Pro to suggest five products in each. The researchers collected the citations, checked domain popularity in \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://tranco-list.eu/\",children:\"Tranco\"}),\", looked at the history of suspicious sites in the \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://web.archive.org/\",children:\"Wayback Machine\"}),\", and published the dataset and the analysis scripts.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-1\",id:\"user-content-fnref-1-3\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"1\"})}),(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-3\",id:\"user-content-fnref-3\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"3\"})}),(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-4\",id:\"user-content-fnref-4\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"4\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[(0,e.jsx)(t.strong,{children:\"59.8%\"}),\" of the 7,534 citations pointed at domains ranked below \",(0,e.jsx)(t.strong,{children:\"#100,000 in Tranco\"}),\", and \",(0,e.jsx)(t.strong,{children:\"23.4%\"}),\" at domains outside Tranco's top million.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-1\",id:\"user-content-fnref-1-4\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"1\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.blockquote,{children:[`\n`,(0,e.jsx)(t.p,{children:\"Obscure does not mean unreliable. Tranco measures popularity, and a specialised engineering blog can answer a technical question better than a large media site. Trellner makes the same distinction.\"}),`\n`]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[\"Among the frequently cited sources, \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://www.g2.com/\",children:\"G2\"}),\" was cited 291 times and \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://www.reddit.com/\",children:\"Reddit\"}),\" 261. \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://www.guideflow.com/\",children:\"Guideflow\"}),\" appeared 194 times, ahead of \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://www.gartner.com/\",children:\"Gartner\"}),\" at 158. \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://www.wikipedia.org/\",children:\"Wikipedia\"}),\" appeared three times.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-1\",id:\"user-content-fnref-1-5\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"1\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[\"Guideflow is the example that interests me most. It sells \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://www.guideflow.com/product/interactive-demo\",children:\"interactive product-demo software\"}),\" and is not a software review publication, yet the study found it cited in 96 of the 380 categories, including some it does not compete in.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-1\",id:\"user-content-fnref-1-6\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"1\"})}),(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-5\",id:\"user-content-fnref-5\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"5\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[\"Nothing suggests Guideflow did anything deceptive. It did ordinary SaaS content marketing: comparison articles, category pages and other material written to attract buyers from search. An AI retrieval system then treated that material as evidence for a much wider range of software-buying questions.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-1\",id:\"user-content-fnref-1-7\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"1\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsx)(t.h2,{id:\"15128-best-software-pages\",children:\"215,128 \\u201Cbest software\\u201D pages\"}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[\"The unusual domains in the dataset were WifiTalents, WorldMetrics and Gitnux. Trellner found signs of common control: registration dates close together, the same pair of \",(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"https://www.cloudflare.com/\",children:\"Cloudflare\"}),\" nameservers, and very similar page structures and content taxonomies. That is circumstantial evidence, and it does not prove ownership.\",(0,e.jsx)(t.sup,{children:(0,e.jsx)(t.a,{href:\"#user-content-fn-1\",id:\"user-content-fnref-1-8\",\"data-footnote-ref\":!0,\"aria-describedby\":\"footnote-label\",children:\"1\"})})]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsxs)(t.p,{children:[\"The size of the operation is not in doubt. Their sitemaps listed \",(0,e.jsx)(t.strong,{children:\"70,731\"}),\", \",(0,e.jsx)(t.strong,{children:\"71,684\"}),\" and \",(0,e.jsx)(t.strong,{children:\"72,713\"}),\" URLs matching this pattern:\"]}),`\n`,(0,e.jsx)(a,{children:(0,e.jsx)(n,{language:\"text\",code:\"/best/\x3Csomet